  "body": "Part of #904 (its point 3).\n\nA STEP file in metres stops at the kernel's least tolerance, 1e-5 m = 0.01 mm (#839). Since #864 it is flagged reduced fidelity (0.005 mm past the importer's promise), so every gouge and collision law runs with half its 0.01 mm tolerance, and an operation held tighter than 0.005 mm is refused (#904's per-kind floor).\n\n**What is owed.** Scale the geometry to millimetres before meshing, so the kernel's least tolerance is 1e-5 mm and a metre file meets the promise like a millimetre file does. #864's decision record notes why it was not done there: it means transforming the kernel's shell before tessellation, which was not small or clearly safe. #917 (STEP through solidcore) may change where this is done; check it first.\n\n**Done means:** `testdata/models/sample_ap214.step` (metres) imports with no reduced-fidelity flag and the same facets, to tolerance, as its millimetre twin would give; or the limit stays, with the reason recorded.\n",
